 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their demand (32) is framed by As-Sa'di. 34:9-14 carries As-Sa'di's reason «لردكم الحق», so Allah's will is not misread. 35: the tafsirs differ on who is meant (Nuh, or the Prophet ﷺ as an aside): no gloss names him and nothing is drawn; only the neutral «كل عليه وزره». Geometric for «إنما يأتيكم به الله إن شاء» and «إن كان الله يريد… هو ربكم». STAGING v4: Nuh is a blue drop labelled Nuh; the chiefs three faceless men in dark robes in a plain town by day. c1 (32): the chiefs speak (32:1), the camera on them after his name, they shake their heads on 32:6 (you have argued too much) and challenge him on 32:7 (bring what you threaten, framed by As-Sa'di's gloss); nothing is acted on the conditional 32:10-13, the camera goes wide. c2 (33-34): Nuh answers (33:1, 34:1) with wide holds only (no close-up during a prophet's words, nobody else gestures); geometric for only Allah brings it if He wills (33:2-7) and for if Allah wills to leave you astray, He is your Lord (34:9-16, with As-Sa'di's reason in the gloss). c3 (35) stays ambient on a night sky: the tafsirs differ on who is meant (Nuh, or the Prophet ﷺ in an aside), and 35:4-12 is a commanded reply, so nobody is drawn; the background stays quiet over 35:4-12."
 },
